! Escudero-Sanz and Navarro wide-angle eye (1999)
! Generated by EveryEyeModel scripts/make_formats.py from data/; do not edit.
! Written by AI (Claude, by Anthropic) at Dan Gray's direction; values from the source below.
! Source: I. Escudero-Sanz and R. Navarro, J. Opt. Soc. Am. A 16(8), 1881-1891 (1999); values as in the ZOSPy example implementation. Cross-checked against Atchison and Smith (2000), appendix A3, which tabulates the 1985 Navarro eye this model is built on: radii, conics, the first three thicknesses, the retina radius and the 589.3 nm indices agree, and so does the power, 60.416 D. The vitreous differs by design: the 1999 model refocuses at 543 nm, and 16.3203 mm is the paraxial focus there. The indices at 458, 543 and 632.8 nm are not in that appendix and remain unchecked against the paper. See models/escudero-sanz-navarro-wide-angle-eye.md.
! Indices are published at four wavelengths; the design wavelength is 543 nm.
! The stop (iris) is placed at the lens front surface, as in common implementations.
LEN NEW
TITLE 'Escudero-Sanz and Navarro wide-angle eye (1999)'
DIM M
EPD 4
WL 458 543 589.3 632.8
REF 2
XAN 0 0 0 0
YAN 0 20 40 60
PRV
PWL 458 543 589.3 632.8
'ESN_COR' 1.382800 1.377700 1.376000 1.374700
'ESN_AQU' 1.344500 1.339100 1.337400 1.336000
'ESN_LEN' 1.429200 1.422200 1.420000 1.418300
'ESN_VIT' 1.342800 1.337700 1.336000 1.334700
END
SO 0 1E+20
S 7.72 0.55 ESN_COR
  CON
  K -0.26
S 6.5 3.05 ESN_AQU
S 10.2 4.0 ESN_LEN
  CON
  K -3.1316
  STO
S -6.0 16.3203 ESN_VIT
  CON
  K -1.0
SI -12.0 0
GO
